Looking at the graph, the function is a downward-opening parabola with x-intercepts at x = -2 and x = 4, so its vertex (the peak) lies at x = 1. The curve reaches its highest point there, at y = 4 (consistent with f(x) = -4/9(x+2)(x-4), which gives f(1) = 4, f(0) = f(2) ≈ 3.56 as shown).

Since the function increases before x = 1 and decreases after, the local maximum value is the y-coordinate of the vertex.

\boxed{4}
